// Package sha256 hashes text with SHA-256 (FIPS 180-4; docs/spec/
// stdlib.md, encodings and digests; G3 std-digest). It is Go's
// crypto/sha256 over Ergo's strings, which hold bytes (types.md, Strings
// 1). Effect has no hash module; Gleam's gleam/crypto and Elixir's
// :crypto.hash/2 give the digest as bytes, as this one does. The extern
// binds a pure runtime/v1 body (runtime/v1/digest.go).

// Sum is the SHA-256 digest of the bytes of s: 32 raw bytes, as Go's
// Sum256. hex.Encode(Sum(s)) is its usual text.
extern go ergo.local/prototype/runtime/v1.Sha256Sum func Sum(s string) string

// SumIs32Bytes: every digest is 32 bytes.
law SumIs32Bytes(s string) { len(Sum(s)) == 32 }
